WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.567 --> 00:00:03.834
-Thank you for being here.
It so nice to see you again.

00:00:03.834 --> 00:00:05.767
This is the first time
meeting you in person.

00:00:05.767 --> 00:00:07.367
-I know.
-You were nice enough to do

00:00:07.367 --> 00:00:08.834
a Zoom with us last time.
-Yeah.

00:00:08.834 --> 00:00:12.467
-And I appreciate that. Is this
your first press tour in person?

00:00:12.467 --> 00:00:14.801
-It is. It is my first
press tour in person.

00:00:14.801 --> 00:00:17.567
And even doing the walk out here
is quite scary.

00:00:17.567 --> 00:00:20.234
You're like, "I don't know
how to walk places."

00:00:20.234 --> 00:00:21.701
[ Laughter ]

00:00:21.701 --> 00:00:23.667
-You forgot how to really walk?
-I've forgotten how to walk.

00:00:23.667 --> 00:00:25.667
When you think about it too
much, it's quite, like --

00:00:25.667 --> 00:00:26.734
it's a strange thing, you know?

00:00:26.734 --> 00:00:28.334
You over sort of think
everything.

00:00:28.334 --> 00:00:30.767
But anyway, yeah, it's lovely
to be in person, finally.

00:00:30.767 --> 00:00:32.300
-Yeah, I'm happy
that you're here.

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:34.968
I know you've done -- you're
doing -- You're so busy.

00:00:34.968 --> 00:00:36.367
You're doing
all these movies now.

00:00:36.367 --> 00:00:38.267
You haven't been to London
in a while,

00:00:38.267 --> 00:00:39.334
which is where you're from?

00:00:39.334 --> 00:00:41.367
-Last year, I wasn't there.

00:00:41.367 --> 00:00:43.667
Well, I was there
for about 10 days-ish.

00:00:43.667 --> 00:00:46.467
-I wanted to make you feel
at home,

00:00:46.467 --> 00:00:51.467
so I got some of your favorite
crisps from England.

00:00:51.467 --> 00:00:53.200
-Oh!
-Now, these are --

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:54.501
I don't know
if I've ever had these.

00:00:54.501 --> 00:00:56.067
What are these?
-Oh, my gosh.

00:00:56.067 --> 00:00:57.901
Okay, so these are Hula Hoops.

00:00:57.901 --> 00:00:59.834
-Has anyone had these?

00:00:59.834 --> 00:01:01.467
-You ever had Hula Hoops?
[ Cheers ]

00:01:01.467 --> 00:01:03.167
-Yeah, five people are familiar
with Hula Hoops. Yeah.

00:01:03.167 --> 00:01:04.601
-We got a whoop for Hula Hoops.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:04.601 --> 00:01:06.334
-What are they?

00:01:06.334 --> 00:01:08.167
-Hula Hoops are
a circular crisp.

00:01:08.167 --> 00:01:10.300
[ Laughter ]

00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:12.300
-A circular crisp.
-And it's almost looks like --

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:14.000
So, you know,
when you're in primary school,

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:16.267
you put them all
on your fingers, like rings,

00:01:16.267 --> 00:01:18.100
and then you eat them off.

00:01:18.100 --> 00:01:19.801
-Oh, that's fun. Yeah.
-It's so much fun.

00:01:19.801 --> 00:01:21.434
-Do you have a favorite flavor?
What should I go with?

00:01:21.434 --> 00:01:23.434
-I would say
the traditional would

00:01:23.434 --> 00:01:25.300
be an already salted Hula Hoop.

00:01:25.300 --> 00:01:26.901
-Alright, so this is
an original. Here we go.

00:01:26.901 --> 00:01:28.667
This is my first Hula Hoop.

00:01:28.667 --> 00:01:31.234
I've never had this.

00:01:31.234 --> 00:01:33.334
-So funny for hula hoops.

00:01:33.334 --> 00:01:34.734
-That's what they look like.
Okay.

00:01:34.734 --> 00:01:36.334
-You got to put it on
your fingers first.

00:01:36.334 --> 00:01:37.501
-Of course, yeah.

00:01:37.501 --> 00:01:38.834
I don't know if they'll fit on
my fingers.

00:01:38.834 --> 00:01:39.968
[ Laughter ]

00:01:39.968 --> 00:01:41.100
I think you were a little --

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:43.234
you were a little girl
when you did this.

00:01:43.234 --> 00:01:44.534
Alright.

00:01:44.534 --> 00:01:47.901
♪♪

00:01:47.901 --> 00:01:50.534
Oh, yeah. These are phenomenal.

00:01:50.534 --> 00:01:53.901
No, no, I love it.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:53.901 --> 00:01:56.033
No, I love these.
-You like?

00:01:56.033 --> 00:01:57.133
-Yeah.
-Oh, good.

00:01:57.133 --> 00:01:59.300
-That might be
my new favorite thing.

00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:01.534
Hula Hoops, I love these.

00:02:01.534 --> 00:02:03.334
These are great. I'm into these.

00:02:03.334 --> 00:02:05.701
What are these?
-These are Quavers.

00:02:05.701 --> 00:02:06.934
-What's Quavers?

00:02:06.934 --> 00:02:09.968
-Quavers are a cheesy,
curled crisp.

00:02:09.968 --> 00:02:12.467
-Are you just reading the bag?
[ Laughter ]

00:02:12.467 --> 00:02:15.167
These are circular.
So this is cheesy curled.

00:02:15.167 --> 00:02:17.000
Now, you don't put these on
your fingers?

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:19.234
-You can do if you want to.
They might fit better.

00:02:19.234 --> 00:02:20.801
-This might fit better
than the other ones.

00:02:20.801 --> 00:02:22.701
This actually fits my finger
more than the --

00:02:22.701 --> 00:02:24.234
[ Laughter ]

00:02:24.234 --> 00:02:26.267
Yeah. Alright, here we go.

00:02:26.267 --> 00:02:27.834
Here we go.

00:02:30.434 --> 00:02:32.601
What in the world?
-You like?

00:02:32.601 --> 00:02:37.033
[ Applause ]

00:02:37.033 --> 00:02:38.767
-Try these, man, Quavers.
Quavers.

00:02:38.767 --> 00:02:40.267
-Quavers?
-Quavers.

00:02:42.534 --> 00:02:43.767
-Wow!

00:02:43.767 --> 00:02:45.434
-That's what I'm talking about,
dude. Come on.

00:02:45.434 --> 00:02:48.734
I don't mess around, dude.

00:02:48.734 --> 00:02:51.767
Well, I wanted to maybe have you
try something

00:02:51.767 --> 00:02:55.367
that you haven't tried,
so I talked to your publicist.

00:02:55.367 --> 00:02:58.300
And I said, "Is there -- Can I
just name some things that maybe

00:02:58.300 --> 00:03:00.234
Daisy hasn't tried?"

00:03:00.234 --> 00:03:03.100
And I found out that you'd never
had Girl Scout cookies.

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:04.634
[ Audience oohs ]
-No.

00:03:04.634 --> 00:03:07.667
-This is a very American thing,
and we love the Girl Scouts.

00:03:07.667 --> 00:03:10.400
Now, it's a big debate of
which is the best one.

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:12.834
Of course,
I have my personal fave.

00:03:12.834 --> 00:03:14.834
-What are they?
What are the differences?

00:03:14.834 --> 00:03:16.467
-Well, alright, look.
Take a peek.

00:03:16.467 --> 00:03:18.834
This one here is --

00:03:18.834 --> 00:03:21.100
Oh, yeah, Caramel deLites
is what they're called now.

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:23.367
They had a different name
when I was growing up.

00:03:23.367 --> 00:03:26.934
This is Caramel deLites.
It's like, coconut, caramel.

00:03:26.934 --> 00:03:30.200
It's unbelievable.
These are peanut butter patties.

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:32.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:32.234 --> 00:03:33.968
Getting some --
The crowd loves that.

00:03:33.968 --> 00:03:35.601
Peanut butter sandwich.

00:03:35.601 --> 00:03:37.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:37.167 --> 00:03:38.434
And then Thin Mint.

00:03:38.434 --> 00:03:41.200
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:43.100
Alright, wait,
so where would you go?

00:03:43.100 --> 00:03:44.501
Would you go --
-Well, I --

00:03:44.501 --> 00:03:47.133
-This is -- The caramel one
would be what I would order.

00:03:47.133 --> 00:03:50.000
-That's yours?
-Yeah.

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:52.501
-I feel like whoop was
quite loud for the mint.

00:03:52.501 --> 00:03:53.734
-Yeah, it was. Yeah.

00:03:53.734 --> 00:03:55.267
So let's try --
Should we try the Thin Mints?

00:03:55.267 --> 00:03:57.267
-I'd be happy to try that too.
-Yeah.

00:03:57.267 --> 00:03:58.801
Why don't you try
that one first?

00:03:58.801 --> 00:04:00.534
Because I feel like
I know the answer.

00:04:00.534 --> 00:04:02.200
[ Laughter ]

00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:03.734
It's going to be probably
Thin Mints, so yeah.

00:04:03.734 --> 00:04:06.968
-Is there a big source of debate
what the best one is?

00:04:06.968 --> 00:04:08.033
-Yes.
-Okay.

00:04:08.033 --> 00:04:09.534
-Yes.
You can try a bite of this.

00:04:09.534 --> 00:04:10.868
You're going to freak out.

00:04:10.868 --> 00:04:12.534
Yeah, you can put it on
your finger if you want to.

00:04:12.534 --> 00:04:14.133
[ Laughter ]

00:04:14.133 --> 00:04:16.133
Out of all of these,
that's the most wearable. Yeah.

00:04:16.133 --> 00:04:18.767
-Okay.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:18.767 --> 00:04:21.200
Oh!

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:22.901
-Right?

00:04:22.901 --> 00:04:24.667
That's something.
It's like a macaroon.

00:04:24.667 --> 00:04:26.300
-Yeah.
-It's not bad, right?

00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:27.434
-I'm surprised, actually.

00:04:27.434 --> 00:04:28.801
-You're surprised?
You enjoy these?

00:04:28.801 --> 00:04:30.434
-It didn't look as appetizing
as it is.

00:04:30.434 --> 00:04:32.534
-Yes, thank you.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:32.534 --> 00:04:34.133
You're not supposed
to look at them, really.

00:04:34.133 --> 00:04:35.267
Okay, here we go.

00:04:35.267 --> 00:04:36.968
The Thin Mints.

00:04:36.968 --> 00:04:40.801
I mean, I didn't know they come
in two tubes of like --

00:04:40.801 --> 00:04:42.033
Alright, get ready.

00:04:42.033 --> 00:04:44.033
I already kind of know.
This is -- Yeah.

00:04:44.033 --> 00:04:46.033
-Okay.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:46.033 --> 00:04:48.033
Alright.
-Yep, here we go.

00:04:48.033 --> 00:04:49.901
Daisy Edgar-Jones.

00:04:53.801 --> 00:04:55.968
Yeah, basic. Right?

00:04:55.968 --> 00:04:57.767
Wait, wait. Hold it, wow.

00:04:57.767 --> 00:04:59.434
Wait a second. Look at this.

00:04:59.434 --> 00:05:01.834
I've never seen this. Wait.
What do you mean "that"?

00:05:01.834 --> 00:05:03.400
Mine?

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:04.834
Yes, exactly right!

00:05:04.834 --> 00:05:06.267
Oh, I love it!

00:05:06.267 --> 00:05:08.634
I love you! Come on!
That's exactly right.

00:05:08.634 --> 00:05:10.767
Thank you. Thank you very much.

00:05:10.767 --> 00:05:12.601
These are the best ones.

00:05:12.601 --> 00:05:14.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:14.267 --> 00:05:16.133
I love you, Girl Scouts.

00:05:16.133 --> 00:05:18.033
I always support
the Girl Scouts.

00:05:18.033 --> 00:05:19.367
But I love you love mine. Good.

00:05:19.367 --> 00:05:20.667
Yeah, I love Thin Mints.

00:05:20.667 --> 00:05:22.534
The secret, though, right,
you freeze them. Right?

00:05:22.534 --> 00:05:24.567
[ Audience shouts "yeah" ]
Yeah, that's the secret thing.

00:05:24.567 --> 00:05:26.667
If you freeze a Thin Mint,
it's a whole different ride.

00:05:28.267 --> 00:05:30.801
I want to talk about your film,
"Fresh."

00:05:30.801 --> 00:05:32.868
Can we talk about this?

00:05:32.868 --> 00:05:34.901
This is getting great reviews,

00:05:34.901 --> 00:05:36.434
by the way, so congratulations
on that.

00:05:36.434 --> 00:05:39.133
[ Applause ]

00:05:39.133 --> 00:05:41.567
It's better not to know anything
beforehand though?

00:05:41.567 --> 00:05:44.167
-I think so.
I think the joy of the film is

00:05:44.167 --> 00:05:47.100
coming to it not knowing where
it goes because it really

00:05:47.100 --> 00:05:49.968
does go on quite a journey.
-Yeah.

00:05:49.968 --> 00:05:52.334
-But, yeah, I would describe it
as a sort of --

00:05:52.334 --> 00:05:56.067
a social thriller about
the perils of modern dating.

00:05:56.067 --> 00:05:57.968
That's kind of one way
you could describe it.

00:05:57.968 --> 00:05:59.133
But yeah.
It's one of the things too.

00:05:59.133 --> 00:06:04.133
-Yeah.
It's -- but it's -- it's dark.

00:06:04.133 --> 00:06:05.267
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:06:05.267 --> 00:06:06.534
-But I don't want to ruin it.
-Yeah.

00:06:06.534 --> 00:06:09.033
-It's dating. But it's -- Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:06:09.033 --> 00:06:10.801
-And Adam McKay --
did he produce it?

00:06:10.801 --> 00:06:12.167
-He did. Yeah, he was
one of the producers.

00:06:12.167 --> 00:06:13.801
-I love Adam McKay.
But this -- it goes --

00:06:13.801 --> 00:06:16.601
Like, you do not see
where this goes at all.

00:06:16.601 --> 00:06:19.000
And then it goes for --
I mean, it's a good --

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:20.634
You get a full ride.
-Yeah.

00:06:20.634 --> 00:06:22.934
-Yeah, you're amazing in it.
It's really, really well done.

00:06:22.934 --> 00:06:24.234
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:06:24.234 --> 00:06:28.100
Here's Daisy Edgar-Jones
and Sebastian Stan in "Fresh."

00:06:28.100 --> 00:06:29.467
Take a look at this.

00:06:29.467 --> 00:06:34.701
-I hate, like, dating, you know?

